From caab1fe05ff69a8bb3c0f3c12b18303a762c60dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:59:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/23] UML-ANDROID-LOCAL: Label the UML GPU sysfs device

libdrm resolves both /dev/dri/card0 and /dev/dri/renderD128 through the
virtio-uml platform device.  Mesa EGL enumerates render nodes with
drmGetDevices2(), which reads the device subsystem link and the drm/
directory as well as uevent.  Labelling uevent alone left those generic
sysfs, so SurfaceFlinger could not classify the device, found no DRM
device, and aborted with "no suitable EGLConfig found".

genfscon matches by prefix, so label the whole GPU platform device.

Change-Id: Ie8b8d414821a0ca31e3284443576e7359da4043b
---
 vsoc_uml_arm64_pgagnostic/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 vsoc_uml_arm64_pgagnostic/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts

diff --git a/vsoc_uml_arm64_pgagnostic/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts b/vsoc_uml_arm64_pgagnostic/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3cf4ea7d5dc5c9739224378c189c36d39f96bf61
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vsoc_uml_arm64_pgagnostic/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# libdrm resolves both /dev/dri/card0 and /dev/dri/renderD128 through this
+# platform device.  Mesa EGL enumerates render nodes with drmGetDevices2(),
+# which reads the device subsystem link and the drm/ directory as well as
+# uevent, so labelling uevent alone leaves SurfaceFlinger unable to classify
+# the device: it finds no DRM device, eglInitialize() fails, and it aborts
+# with "no suitable EGLConfig found".  genfscon matches by prefix, so label
+# the whole GPU platform device.
+genfscon sysfs /devices/virtio-uml-cmdline/virtio-uml.0 u:object_r:sysfs_gpu:s0
